From 1bc1de6ac2633713ea9da43a410d3a6670a29fee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:35:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(view): Back, Left and Bottom views on the View menu

The README's "not yet" list had Back and Bottom. ViewId, VIEWS and
VIEW_DIRS carry back (looking along -Y), left (along +X) and bottom
(looking up +Z with +Y up the screen: the plan seen through the floor,
so +X runs left), each a square parallel view framed like the others.
They are on the View menu as "Back view", "Left view" and "Bottom
view"; the top bar keeps the mock's five buttons (BAR_VIEWS), and a
menu view lights none of them. The guide says where each view lives.

Tests: camera.test.ts (the eight views and their projections, the
bar's five, every direction, opposite pairs cancel, square views' up is
square to their direction), navigation.spec.ts (each menu view sets
data-view and a parallel projection with no bar button pressed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DaoaGXWjtprTCuXM54m2KR
